      "rationale": "The lowest, most obliquely ascending fibres act mainly as an adductor. They assist extension only from a flexed position, as in a dip or pullover. The shoulder-girdle depression is indirect, acting via the humerus, so it is kept minor. No shoulder_position_hold role is given because it does not resist the shoulder-extension moment of a curl or hold the arm overhead.",
