      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "It is a major shoulder flexor alongside the anterior deltoid and a strong horizontal adductor, as in an incline press. It adducts only with the arm below about 90 degrees, so adduction is weighted lower than for the sternocostal head. As a shoulder flexor it assists the anterior deltoid isometrically in resisting the shoulder-extension moment that keeps the upper arm still in a curl.",
      "status": "reviewed"
